hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27996","Rawh narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Amr ibn Muadh al-Ashhali, from his grandmother, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O believing women, let none of you despise for her neighbor, even a burnt sheep trotter."
"27997","Rawh narrated to us: Malik informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Bijayd al-Ansari, from his grandmother, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Return the beggar, even with a burnt hoof."
"27998","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Zayd, from Amr ibn Muadh al-Ansari, he said: A beggar stood at their door, and his grandmother Hawwa said to him: Feed him dates. They said: We have none. She said: Then give him sawiq drink. They said: Wonder at you; can we feed him what we do not have. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Do not return the beggar, even with a burnt hoof."
